# Compiled output. Per-package, therefore `**/`, not root-anchored: `nx
# build` writes to packages/*/dist, and Jest writes coverage to
# packages/*/test-output/jest/coverage. Same distinction eslint.config.mjs's
# ignores block makes (dist/out-tsc/coverage there too), applied here for
# the same reason.
**/dist
**/out-tsc

# Nx — only ever created at the workspace root, so root-anchored is correct.
/.nx/cache
/.nx/workspace-data

# Verdaccio's local registry storage — package.json's `local-registry`
# target writes to tmp/local-registry/storage, a root-only path, unlike
# dist/out-tsc/coverage above.
/tmp

# Generiert
**/plugin-registry.ts
# Always join(workspaceRoot, 'ng-prism-cache') — never per-package, so
# root-anchored is correct (see eslint.config.mjs's ignores block).
/ng-prism-cache

# Coverage
**/coverage
# Written only by `npm run test:coverage` to this one fixed path, read by the
# coverage plugin — not a per-package pattern, so root-anchored is correct.
/test-workspace/coverage

# Lokale Notizen (global gitignored) — only ever at the workspace root.
/.claude
/.superpowers
/.posts
